{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1340017-ideas-for-a-large-spiritual-quest","id":1340017,"title":"Ideas for a large spiritual quest?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-07T05:40:50-07:00","id":1340017,"title":"Ideas for a large spiritual quest?","content":"My game is already 52 game session in, and the PCs are a Rank 4 Guhral, a Rank 3 Bastet and a Rank 3 Garu. Their goal is uniting the changing breeds to face the Final Battle together.<br /> <br /> Most of my game has developed so far in the real world, using the Umbra just like a tool to access places. They have played the Foundation Valkenberg adventures, they fought the Zenit Gregornous Deathwing in Russia (with canon results) and they\u2019ve just become a key element in defeating BlackTooth, the Ahadi is in good shape (better than Canon).<br /> Now I want to focus the Game in a big Umbral adventure. Their goal is finding Mokole-Membe himself and convince him to join with his progeny the War against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> So ideas for PCs adventures in their path to Mokole-Membe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T18:41:45-07:00","id":1340127,"title":"","content":"Rage Across the Heaven's and Umbra Revised, have them start with a trip to the Abyss to find some sort of apocryphal map or scroll/journal or even a bird spirit that used to clean the dragon's teeth. Have it then lead them on a trip to the Aetherial Realm. Maybe they have to go and Collect Moonsilver and Sungold to recreate that Electrum spear of Legend and use it as a grand key to open up a Tomb built upon one of Rorg's Astroids, or maybe he slumbers in Pangea or the Legendary Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T19:04:43-07:00","id":1340132,"title":"","content":"Congrats on reaching 52 game sessions. That is a lot of work/<br /> <br /> Well, it seems to me they need to travel to the Near Realm of Pangaea to find Mokole-Membe. That means an epic spirit quest (aisling). (Note, I have not read the Mokole book, so I am only going by being inspired by the actual Congo legend).<br /> <br /> First, they'll need to find a way to get there. That means identifying various spirit clues - starting in the Penumbra - that they follow which gets them deeper and deeper into the Umbra. So to start, where in the Penumbra of today can they actually find something that has the meaning or resonance of the Pangean realm? These paths and signposts are the airts they need to follow. The PCs need to be thinking of spirit significance here, not rational logic.<br /> <br /> How many stages that quest needs to be really depends on how difficult or long you want to make the journey to Pangaea. It could be as little as three or 10+. You also need to determine what happens at each stage. I would start small and then have each subsequent stage be more difficult or longer to resolve and find the next airt.<br /> <br /> So maybe the first stage is just them finding an airt from the local Penumbra to a more appropriate spot in the Penumbra. That may just require PCs to find something(s) of &quot;primal Earth&quot; significance, maybe a low difficulty Wits + Enigmas roll(s), and some ordinary Penumbral encounters along the way. The first stage will also be the prep time the PCs use to prepare themselves for this aisling. This could be anything from gathering resources, to putting their Realm affairs in order to account for their long absence, to spiritual devotions like fasting. I'd also have them do research on the kind of chiminage they'd be expected to pay in order to get his help.<br /> <br /> Second stage might be from Penumbra to a series of umbral Domains (glens) that increasingly represent Pangaea. Each Domain should have its own &quot;story&quot; or challenge that needs to be overcome. The types of challenges should be things where the PCs have to abandon their modern resources and mentalities, and adopt ways appropriate to Pangaea. For skill checks, emphasize Knowledges less and Talents more. Primal Urge should be more important than a skill like Survival. Wits over Intelligence. Slowly have any of their clothing or fetishes fall apart and become useless UNLESS it is something that could exist in only the most ancient part of the Stone Age (even things like bows and arrows, and fishing lines should be too &quot;new&quot; - we're talking stone spears, and leather hide clothes they make themselves without stitches). Personally, I'd keep them going from one Domain to the next Domain, etc. UNTIL their characters &quot;deserve&quot; to enter Pangaea by acting in a way you see appropriate to that place. By the end, they may decide to totally abandon anything homid and survive simply in lupus/hispo mode.<br /> <br /> if the PCs want to &quot;cheat&quot; like find a moon bridge to go on, let them, but then have something HAPPEN en route, and the moon bridge collapses and they get dumped somewhere in the umbra and have to make their way as above. A spirit quest should not be treated like a tool, but an actual spiritual journey that changes the PCs. You'll want to see spiritual growth from the PCs.<br /> <br /> Third stage will be when they have finally earned entrance into Pangaea and they are in the Near Realm, you have more practical adventures where they have to locate Mokole-Membe. These adventrues should always rely on the abilities and mentality they &quot;learned&quot; during the Domain hopping. You don't want them to use the &quot;wrong&quot; abilities and lessons to work here. Read the Pangaea description in the Umbra books, and use it as a sandbox so they can experience it as a setting as they get slowly closer to their goal.<br /> <br /> The fourth stage will be arrival to where Mokole-Membe is and resolve any challenge you have for that encounter. Then they can begin, finally, to attempt to convince the creature to help them. This should require really appropriate chiminage - things that cause permanent changes in the behavior of one or more PCs. Things they have to pay or perform now, combined with promises of new actions to be done later.<br /> <br /> Then having won their prize, they need to figure out the way back. That should be a lot easier, but could be complicated from whatever spiritual enemies they've made along the way or who wants to stop them. But by this point, the players will likely want to quickly get back, so don't make it too hard or long.<br /> <br /> That is the general frame I would use. I think if you can read one of the Umbra books and study up Pangaea (and maybe do some additional &quot;research&quot; by reading old Marvel Comics with the Savage Land, or some Edgar Rice Burroughs novels), you can jot down a list of appropriate scenes, challenges,and encounters you'll want to run during the quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 10-07-2019, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T09:39:27-07:00","id":1340245,"title":"","content":"Damn; Black Fox, nice post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T08:56:00-07:00","id":1340419,"title":"","content":"Yes, indeed. I appreciate a lot the ideas, I'm going to definitely use many of them (I hope my players don't read this forum)<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}